WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.010
- [Instructor] We are told
that Andre goes to a movie

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.410
that starts at 19 hours 45 minutes,

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.310
or 19:45,

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.080
and is 90 minutes long.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.870
What time is the movie finished?

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.160
So pause this video, and
see if you can answer that

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.560
before we work through it together.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.900
All right, so what I like to do is set up

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.110
what we could call a timeline.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.280
So if this is our timeline,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.570
and let's say that this is
19 hours right over here,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.670
19 hours,

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:37.930
maybe this is 20 hours right over there,

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.690
and then this would be 21
hours right over there.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.120
Now, what time does the movie start?

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.060
It starts at 19 hours 45 minutes.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.370
So this would be 19 hours 30 minutes,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.240
which would be halfway
between 19 hours and 20 hours,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.950
and 19 hours 45 minutes

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.510
would be halfway between 19:30 and 20.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.050
So 19 hours and 45 would
be right over there.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.050
So let me write that down.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.020
That is 19 hours and 45 minutes,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:09.920
and that is when this
movie is going to start.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.390
Now, it's going to
continue for 90 minutes.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.180
So when does it end?

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.130
So there's a couple of ways
you could think about it.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:20.800
The way I think about it is
it will take us 15 minutes

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.780
to get to 20 hours, so that's 15 minutes.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.570
And so 15 minutes of the movie
has happened by 20 hours.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.340
And then how much is left?

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.010
Well, 19 minus 15 is 75,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.400
so then there's another 75 minutes left.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.730
Well, 60 of those 75 are gonna
get you to the next hour,

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.870
so then it's going to be like this.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.690
So then you're going to
have another 60 minutes

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.720
to get to the next hour.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.550
So, so far we've used 75,

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.480
and then you're going to
need another 15 minutes

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.600
to have a total of 90 minutes.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.870
So then you're going to
have another 15 minutes.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.200
And so when does the movie end?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.740
Well, as you can see, we started at 19:45,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.120
15 minutes got us to 20,

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.290
another 60 minutes got us to 21,

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.940
so now we have a total of 75.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.720
And then another 15 would
give us a total of 90,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.530
so we are finishing 15 minutes

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.740
after the 21st hour

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.700
or after hour 21 or however
you wanna think about it.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.920
So this time right over here is going

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.100
to be 21 hours and 15 minutes,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.790
or 21:15.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.123
So that's the time that
the movie is finished.

